  "domain": "tier0/export/processing",
  "description": "Item 2.7 unrecorded discriminator for the arithmetic of a far tap's rigid turn (decision 364): six exact folded seam pairs (flat or bent far island, Pythagorean folds), each copied at 27 world offsets from 0 to 200 cm across a mesh box whose normalisation scale and centre are not powers of two, turned 90 degrees, scaled 2 and 3 times in 3D and translated to another UV slot; every position and UV exact in float32, so a double far turn gives every translated copy of a shape the same chain (taps relative to the slot, fractions) and float32 position arithmetic does not; no two copies share a 3D point (tools/parity/fit/padding_world_offset.py); predictions frozen before capture. User0-User7 added as RGB32F (a record whose template capture shows one of them not 32F is void); one fill with the eight channels active, Normal at opacity 1, default projection (read back), sources the authored float32 kernel code at the document size: User0-User2 one-hot the nine classes x mod 3 + 3 (y mod 3) of the texel (column x, row y from the top), User3 the UV ramp R = (x + 0.5)/N, G = (y + 0.5)/N, B = 0.5, User4 and User5 the periodic codes d and e (k/256, one 17 x 13 texel tile each), User6 (d + e)/2 and User7 1 - d. The eight maps at OpenEXR 32f with infinite padding and with passthrough (every covered texel must equal its source bit for bit, or the probe is void), every export step done twice in the session.",
